Lucciola: the brightness keys work on the login screen

The greeter's own compositor handled only the VT switch keys, so the
screen's brightness could not be changed at the login screen. The
brightness keys now step the panel's backlight by 5% (never below 1%),
through logind's SetBrightness on the greeter's session, as a desktop
session does it without root, with systemd's busctl: no new library and
no shell. The backlight is the one the kernel prefers (firmware, then
platform, then raw).

